WEBVTT

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:29.400
My father was a rather unique individual.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.820
He'd be obsessed over
musical instruments I'd never seen.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.990
Rather than putting soy sauce
or <i>tonkatsu </i>sauce on his eggs,

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.030
he'd put ponzu on them.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.740
Hiyori.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.960
Wow, you're using an artificial fly?
That's pretty rare.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.090
Well, Mr. Yamakawa only did fly fishing.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.630
Oh, I guess you're right.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.760
Well, you be careful now, Hiyori.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.060
And this rather unique father of mine

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:06.020
died three years ago due
to a very popular disease.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.780
I don't like dealing
with people I don't know,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:17.530
so I try to make myself seem
as unapproachable as possible.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.830
Looking back, when I was little,

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.200
I used to hide behind my dad all the time.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.920
I should probably head home soon.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.550
It's the ocean!

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:47.560
Wow! It's the real deal!

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.850
It's so big!

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:50.270
--Is she a tourist?
But it's not even summer...

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:55.570
--Wow, this is amazing! It's all sparkly!
--Is she a tourist?
But it's not even summer...

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:56.400
Uh?!

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.070
"Koharu"

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.700
"Koharu"
Is she planning to jump in?

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.120
But it's only March!

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.410
Here I go!

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.080
Wait a sec!

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.620
I have to stop her! I have to stop her!

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.960
I have to stop her!

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.670
"Notice: Do not cast your line at people"

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:15.550
Huh?

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.390
Ow, ow, ow...

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.390
S-Sorry!

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:33.020
Are you okay? Did you get hurt--?

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.690
It's cold...

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:37.610
I'm sure it is...

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:46.040
On this day, a very unique
girl entered into my life.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:57.050
"Episode 1"
"A Very Unique Girl"

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.600
Oh, I feel so much warmer now!

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.310
Let's not try to jump into
the ocean in March again.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.100
Okay!

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.860
So, I'm going to be
moving to this city soon.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.860
I come from a prefecture
where you can't see the ocean at all

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.190
so I got really excited!

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.570
So she's really never
seen the ocean before...

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.660
I guess people like her exist.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.910
Hey, are you from here?

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.290
Yeah, I guess...

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.950
Aw, that's so cool! I'm jealous!

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.830
Wh-What?

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.250
Hey, are those fish?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.920
Yeah, they're called rockfish.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.760
They're pretty easy to catch around here.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.420
You caught them?!

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.510
Y-Yeah...

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.430
Wow! Are you a fisherman?!

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.260
I am not...

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.220
I see.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.850
I guess if she's never seen the ocean

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.480
she's probably never
seen anyone fishing either.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.480
Oh, but hey. I fish all the time, too!

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.440
Oh, really? Like river fishing?

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.940
Nope.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:00.150
Through video games!

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.440
"Whoever catches the heaviest Sea Nyan wins"

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.440
Through video games!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.860
"Whoever catches the heaviest Sea Nyan wins"

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.860
Virtual fishing?

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.360
Virtual fishing?

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.860
That's a fishing rod, right?

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.660
Y-Yeah.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.370
Did you want to hold it?

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.950
Can I?!

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.920
Wow... A real fishing rod.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.340
And this is...

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:19.920
--...garbage?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.460
--No.
--...garbage?

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.260
This is called an artificial fly.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.720
It's basically artificial bait
that's made to look like a little fish.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.430
Usually, you'd use bugs.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:28.930
Artificial bait?

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.810
Aren't those usually made out of plastic?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.060
Are you talking about lures?

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.520
Yeah, probably those.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:38.360
Well, I guess the average person
wouldn't know what an artificial fly is.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.530
They're about as known as water fleas.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.820
Oh, water fleas are super famous!
We learn about them in science class!

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:45.860
That's not exactly what I meant.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.370
This is the only way to fish
that my father taught me.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.870
Hey!

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.540
I want to see you catch something!

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.050
Huh? R-Right now?

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:05.260
Right now! I've only ever
seen people catch fish on TV.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.970
Then you want to help me
catch one with this landing net?

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:10.810
Landing?

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:15.690
I'll lure the fish over here and
then you'll use that to scoop it up.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.480
Totally!

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.410
Huh? Wha--?!

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.200
Why are you teasing them like that?!

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:34.500
I'm not. Remember when
we talked about lures?

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.120
Yeah.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:40.290
Those kinds of artificial lures are heavy
so you can actually feel them go flying.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.000
I sorta get it!

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.300
And well... I've only
ever done fly fishing...

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.840
See? Artificial flies are small
and light, so if you just

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:50.890
cast it normally, it won't go very far.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:52.140
Huh...

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.810
And so, you use these fly lines.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.140
Ooh!

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:59.270
These lines are thicker
and heavier than normal lines.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:04.730
You use the weight of the line and imagine
the artificial fly going far and...

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.070
Ooh! It flew!

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:12.240
I wonder how many meters that was. I can't
see the artificial fly at all anymore!

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.240
Wow!

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.950
Come to think of it,

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:18.460
this might be the first time I've talked
this much with someone I've just met.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.080
Especially about fishing.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.090
I got a bite!

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.340
Wha--?!

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.880
Something actually ate
that piece of garbage?

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.510
Are you just looking for a fight?

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.760
More importantly, come on. Use the net.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.680
Huh? Right now?

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.220
Yes, now!

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.640
Hurry!

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.770
Hi-yah!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.830
Whoa, it's moving!
This fish is so alive right now!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.910
Calm down.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:07:00.210
Wow... We really caught one.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.000
Hey, is this fish edible?

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.800
Well, I was planning on
bringing it home with me,

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.300
but you want me to turn it
into sashimi right here?

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.970
You can do that?!

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:15.010
Y-Yeah. My dad taught me how.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.770
First, you take some scissors and...

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:19.520
"Fresh Wasabi"

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:19.520
First, you take some scissors and...

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:20.690
"Fresh Wasabi"

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:20.690
Scissors?

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:25.570
The fins on a rockfish are pointy and
dangerous, so you cut them off first.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.190
Huh...

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:31.360
And you used to be so edgy...

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.450
When did you two get so close?

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.740
Next, you chop off the head
and pull out the guts with it.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:38.790
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:42.170
And then you cut along its spine.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.500
I see.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:49.760
You get rid of the belly bones,
peel off the skin, slice it up and...

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.340
And there you go. Fresh rockfish sashimi.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:57.010
Wow! That's amazing! Are you a chef?

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:57.100
I am not.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.310
"No hesitation"

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.310
I am not.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:07:58.720
I am not.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.780
I think she's trying
to tell me it's delicious.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:15.030
It's sorta crunchy.
It's definitely hard to chew!

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.700
Oh, that's because
it's going through rigor mortis.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:18.620
Rigor...?

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:23.250
Fish are like humans
and go through rigor mortis.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:27.250
When you put it like that, it feels
like we did something heinous.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.000
"Alibi" "Rigor mortis"

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.000
When you put it like that, it feels
like we did something heinous.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:28.340
"Alibi" "Rigor mortis"

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:28.340
"Motive: Because I wanted to eat it..."
When you put it like that, it feels
like we did something heinous.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.010
"Motive: Because I wanted to eat it..."

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:32.300
"Motive: Because I wanted to eat it..."
I definitely don't feel that.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.220
I definitely don't feel that.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.220
Thanks for the meal.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.850
So this is how something
tastes fresh out of the water.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.390
Fishing is so fun and delicious!

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:43.560
If I knew it'd make her this happy,

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.860
I wish I'd learned other
dishes other than sashimi.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.440
I've never had rockfish sashimi before.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.360
I usually just stew them.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.320
Wait, you can cook?!

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.990
And I'm really good at it, too!
Though I've never tried to make sashimi.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.240
I definitely wasn't expecting that.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.830
I live alone with my dad,
and we both take turns doing chores.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.880
But my dad's terrible at cooking
so I just make all the food.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.670
Ah, so he's the opposite of my dad.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:12.050
Hey! Do you always hang out around here?

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.300
Yeah, well... Not all the time.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:18.050
Then next time,
I'll bring my cooking tools.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:22.390
So you'll catch them, and I'll cook them.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.310
It'll be so much fun!

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:30.770
She really is such a strange girl.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.070
Oh, I should get home.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.360
Do you have a curfew?

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:41.910
No, but... My mom's
getting remarried and tonight,

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:46.160
I'm having dinner with them and their kid.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:49.290
Well...

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:53.510
My dad died from
an illness three years ago.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.760
I'm meeting this new person
for the first time today

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.180
so I've been wondering what they're like.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:02.180
I got so anxious, so I came to the ocean.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:06.520
But I think I feel a little better
after hanging out with you.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:07.810
Thanks.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:11.310
Wow, what a coincidence.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:15.820
I'm also having dinner with the person
my dad is remarrying and her kid tonight.

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:17.030
Huh?

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:22.200
Do things like this actually happen?!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.830
It's nice to meet you! I'm Koharu Minagi!

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.500
And I'm her father, Issei.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.160
I'm Hiyori's mother, Hinata.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.040
I-I'm Hiyori...

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.380
You're the fishing person!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.420
What a crazy coincidence!

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.840
Oh, you two already know each other?

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:38.880
Yeah! We're super close!
We even ate fish together.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.760
Oh, my.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.890
I can't wait to get to
know you better, Hiyori!

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:51.980
My new sister...

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.190
--Daddy, I'll make us some
stewed rockfish for dinner!

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:55.320
--...is a rather unique girl.
--Daddy, I'll make us some
stewed rockfish for dinner!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.280
--...is a rather unique girl.
--Let's go to Hiyori's place!

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.990
Uh, but we've already
reserved a restaurant.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.990
Oh, dear...

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.670
Hiyori! I think they're here!

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.790
Okay, got it.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.470
Hello! I guess we'll be living
under the same roof starting today!

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:25.430
Welcome. I've been really
looking forward to this.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:28.270
"Koi"
"The Minagis are here"
We can talk later.
Let's get all of our luggage in.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:29.730
"Koi"
"The Minagis are here"
Okay!

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:32.190
"Koi"
"The Minagis are here"
Oh, are they moving in today?

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:34.980
Yeah. We're about to
get all their boxes in.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:38.820
So I guess you're going from
Hiyori Yamakawa to Hiyori Minagi.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.990
Yeah. It still doesn't feel real, but...

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:43.700
Hiyori, come help us out.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.370
Coming!

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:49.870
"A few days later"

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:56.630
I feel so much older wearing a necktie.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.960
Hiyori! Come here for a sec!

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.130
What's up?

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:05.470
Look, look! I bought a ribbon!

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:07.970
I think we're supposed to wear
neckties for the entrance ceremony.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:12.690
D'oh! But I stuffed my
necktie deep into that drawer.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:17.110
Also... You should probably
get unpacked already.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.940
Koharu.

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:22.610
We should probably take care
of all the kitchen stuff first.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.820
Oh, right. I forgot.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.950
Sorry that things are so hectic.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:31.330
Your entrance ceremony's this weekend.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.670
N-No, it's fine.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:41.920
Does it bother you that
Koharu took Shinya's room?

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.590
Not at all! It's totally fine!

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.430
But...

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:48.220
I-I mean... Koharu needs a room!

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:52.810
And I heard it's not good
to leave rooms like that as is...

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.560
Hiyori...

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.770
Crap. He's worrying about me.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.650
U-Um!

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.450
I'm going over to a friend's house!
I wanted to show them my uniform!

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:18.210
Hm... I think I've seen this
thing before but what is it?

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:21.630
You can sort things out
however you like, Koharu.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.170
Are you sure?

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:26.550
Neither Hiyori nor I cook that much.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.510
Okay, then I guess I will.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:30.430
Sure, go ahead.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:36.390
Then I wonder if this
belonged to Hiyori's dad, too.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:41.070
Are you sure I can use that room?

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:47.740
Of course. This is your
home now, too, Koharu.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:54.040
Did you not want to use that room?

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:58.290
I-I'm so sorry.
I didn't even consider that.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.790
I-It's totally fine!

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.630
Do you want to switch rooms with Hiyori?

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.880
No, it's really okay.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.850
Hiyori?

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.730
It's really hard to be
at home right now...

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:25.530
I mean... there's not
much I can do about it.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:26.950
But still...

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:34.830
At least the ocean never changes on me.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.160
Hiyori!

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.750
H-How long have you been standing there?

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:45.050
"At least the ocean never changes on me."

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.550
Stop that.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:48.720
So what did you need?

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:51.890
I think you forgot your fishing stuff,
so I brought them for you.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.930
Why do you have a futon whacker?

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.730
I'm not fishing today.
The wind's too strong.

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:58.850
What?!

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:02.020
Come on! Let's do some fishing!
Come on! Come on! Please?!

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:03.980
She's throwing a tantrum...

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:08.700
But it is rare for another girl
to be so interested in fishing.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:09.780
"Happy"

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.450
I guess we can try for a little bit.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:14.240
Yay!

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:21.040
Wait... Did I b-break it
o-on my way over here...?

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.540
Don't worry. They're designed like this.

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.710
You put it together like this.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:30.590
And then you bend the fly line
through the hoop like this...

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:32.180
I wanna try.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.760
Sure.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.850
Piece of cake!

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:38.310
Yeah, good job.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:41.390
Next... hup!

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:45.400
Er, you just need to lay it down.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:47.230
Are you some kind of genius?!

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:50.860
Okay! Fishing time!

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:52.860
Are you planning to bat with that?

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:54.120
How do you do it?

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.620
Are you right or left-handed?

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:56.740
Right!

00:15:56.740 --> 00:16:00.710
Then your right hand goes here,
and your left hand will hold the line.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.580
Ah, I see.

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:05.040
I did it!

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:08.800
I just realized she didn't attach
an artificial fly, but whatever.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:11.130
I'm sure she won't be
able to cast it right anyway.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.930
Okay, here I go!

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:18.390
Ready, and... Hi-yah!

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.110
Huh?

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.690
Of course...

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:28.980
But I swung as hard as I could...

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:31.740
You need to do the opposite.
Don't put any strength into it.

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:33.320
Really?

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.700
I told you before, right?

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:37.280
You need to take advantage
of the weight of the line.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.450
Oh, you're tilting the rod too far back.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:42.370
First you go slow, and then you
whip it really fast at the last second.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:46.130
Oh, you put too much strength into
it again. Lower the rod at the end.

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.590
Make sure you don't
swing it around too much!

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:53.930
Enough armchair theories!

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:55.300
What?!

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:59.140
That's right!
You were teasing the fishies!

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:01.100
I wasn't teasing anything.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.690
It's called false casting.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:04.980
Fal what?

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:09.020
When you cast behind you,
it's called back casting.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:10.230
That's pretty straightforward.

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:13.900
And when you cast in front
of you it's called forward casting.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:14.860
Forward? Like in soccer?

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:20.910
This is when your line will look
like a "tsu" and it's called a loop.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:26.170
When you keep repeating your back
and forward casting to stabilize the loop,

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.250
it's called false casting.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:30.170
Let's have you practice that first.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:31.090
Hiyori... You can speak
Japanese, you know?

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:34.010
"Forward cast" "Back cast" "False cast"

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:34.010
Hiyori... You can speak
Japanese, you know?

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:36.050
"Forward cast" "Back cast" "False cast"

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:36.050
J-Japanese?

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:36.800
J-Japanese?

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:39.850
Swing backwards. Swing forwards.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.470
Then swing back and forth?

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:43.220
That's so easy to understand!

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:47.770
Fly fishing originated from England,
so all the tools have English names, too.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:49.150
England?!

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.070
I see.

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.900
So I just need to feel like a British
person and I'll be able to throw it good.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.530
That's the philosophy you came to?

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:55.400
Gimme!

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.650
O-Okay...

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:01.910
England... Black tea...

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:06.370
Rock... A British gentleman...

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:07.460
I got it!

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:09.380
British Gentleman Throw!

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.800
This is gonna take a while...

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:18.640
But if she's this interested,
I hope she'll find fishing fun.

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:23.810
Maybe I should look up more
beginner ways of fishing for her...

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.480
But...

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.020
Hi-yah!

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:32.440
Why don't we head home?

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:33.730
What?

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:38.490
Even I wouldn't be able to cast well
with the wind being this strong.

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:43.160
Just a little bit more...
Let's just try a little bit more.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:47.160
Did she happen to notice
I was uncomfortable being home?

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.040
One more time!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.210
Nah, let's go home.

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:59.880
Hey, is it awkward living with my dad?

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.010
That was straight to the point.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:04.100
Well... A little.

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:07.430
Do you feel awkward living with my mom?

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:10.850
Hm... Well, maybe a little.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:16.780
Oh, yeah! My name's Koharu, got it?

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:19.200
I'm not "you." I'm Koharu.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:22.570
I am older than you,
but you can just call me Koharu.

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:27.160
Older than me? By like two months...

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.330
Just shut up and say my name.

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.470
K-Koharu...

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.090
Here!

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:49.310
Aw... I really wanted to make dinner
with the fish we caught.

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:51.230
Oh, in that case...

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.570
Are these all fish?

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:56.820
Yeah...

00:19:56.820 --> 00:20:01.570
My mom doesn't cook either and we
sometimes give some to our neighbors....

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:03.570
We just can't eat all of it.

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:07.080
So why do you keep fishing?

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:10.410
B-Because there are fish in the ocean...

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.290
Oh...

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:17.050
There's a lot of sashimi up top, too.

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:18.960
I want some sashimi!

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:25.140
But it might not be as
good anymore. I'll eat those.

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:28.640
Don't worry! A few little tricks
and it'll be delicious again.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.020
What are you going to do? Fry them?

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.560
Non, non!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.480
"Koharu's Kitchen"

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:36.520
"Koharu's Kitchen"
Koharu's Kitchen!

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.190
First, we put the sashimi into a bowl.

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:41.440
Uh-huh.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:46.070
Then we'll add an equal amount
of dashi, soy sauce, and mirin.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.160
I see.

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:50.000
Then we'll throw in
some ground white sesame.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.120
Now what?

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:55.080
Then we're going to throw
that mixture onto some hot rice

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.040
and sprinkle on some small green onions...

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:01.460
Ta-dah! The <i>zukedon </i>is complete!

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:04.340
My dad would make this sometimes.

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:07.010
I had no idea it was so easy to make...

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.430
Go on, eat up!

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:11.640
O-Okay. Thanks for the food.

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:20.900
It's good.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:26.610
I know, right? I make this whenever
we have some leftover sashimi.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:31.540
But the one my dad made
tasted a little different.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:34.290
I wonder if she used
a different soy sauce.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:35.670
But it's really good.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:38.170
Hey, what are you eating?

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:40.960
<i>Zukedon</i>! Do you want some, Dad?

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:42.670
I'd be happy to have some.

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:44.760
It won't take too long.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:47.430
Did you catch this fish, Hiyori?

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:49.390
Oh, uh... Yes.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:51.560
Wow, that's impressive.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:54.680
I got to eat one that she just caught!

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:57.600
Oh, but white-meat fish
tends to taste better

00:21:57.600 --> 00:22:00.770
after a few days rather
than freshly caught.

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:03.320
Huh... I didn't know that.

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:05.700
So you tricked me...

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.740
What in the world are you talking about?

00:22:08.780 --> 00:22:11.280
Despite how she looks,
she had really bad asthma as a kid,

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:13.450
and spent a lot of time in the hospital.

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:18.750
So she never got to play outside much.

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:20.750
I hope you'll show her the ropes.

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:27.720
Come to think of it,

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:32.850
Koharu is going to be living
with a new family in a new city.

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:37.810
Are you awake, Hiyori?

00:22:37.810 --> 00:22:39.400
Yeah.

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:44.820
What's up?

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:49.240
Well, um...

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:55.500
I was just wondering if it's really okay
for me to be using your dad's room...

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:01.630
Oh, is that all?

00:23:01.630 --> 00:23:03.340
Is that all?!

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:08.550
Hey, I'm gonna look into easier ways
of fishing like bait fishing,

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:12.220
so let's go to the ocean again
when the weather's better.

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:15.810
Sure.

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:18.020
But!

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:22.310
I want to get better at fly fishing, too!
So I'm gonna train!

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:25.940
Crap. This is definitely
going to be a handful.

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:29.200
"Minami Kanagawa High School"

00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:36.580
A new uniform, a new school building...

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:41.000
...and a new...

00:23:44.380 --> 00:23:46.090
Let's go!

00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:54.050
I hope we're in the same class!

00:23:55.060 --> 00:23:55.970
"Next Time"

00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:57.310
"Next Time"
Hey, Hiyori.

00:23:57.310 --> 00:24:00.140
"Next Time"
Why are fly lines so colorful?

00:24:00.140 --> 00:24:02.480
"Next Time"
So you can see them
better after you cast them.

00:24:02.480 --> 00:24:04.690
"Next Time"
So you can choose whatever color you want.

00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:06.730
"Next Time"
Then I choose the rainbow-colored one!

00:24:06.730 --> 00:24:09.490
"Next Time"
I'm not sure if that exists...
